## Shared Web implementation checkpoint ΓÇö Trading overlay presentation binding

FCR-0126 Web-owned presentation work has materially advanced.

Implemented:
- provider-neutral overlay presenter for the Application-defined element family: `POINT`, `PRICE_LEVEL`, `HORIZONTAL_LINE`, `VERTICAL_LINE`, `ZONE`, `SERIES`, `MARKER`, `ANNOTATION`;
- non-applicable overlays are not rendered as current Trading truth;
- unknown primitive types fail closed rather than causing Web to recreate Strategy/School logic;
- update application requires exact `OverlayProjectionId` and recognized `ADD|UPDATE|CORRECT|INVALIDATE|REMOVE|STATUS` type;
- market-data series and Trading overlay projection remain separate inputs to visual composition.

Evidence: `applications/shared/web/src/presenters/trading-overlay.js` at commit `11a9830404c1d560df07f46b975875d980a6f873`; focused tests added at `2f4e64885d428bd38fea600ecf5214546fe819e7`.

No Strategy activation, execution authority, runtime route or Application-private access is created.

Checkpoint: `applications/shared/web/docs/FCR_RECONCILIATION_IMPLEMENTATION_CHECKPOINT_03.md` @ `757c7d48fcda17b5b8dbfb886765fe71b1467273`.

Governed executable verification remains pending, therefore no closure claim is made.

`HANDOFF_UPDATE_REQUIRED: Waiting On=WEB; Next Required Action=Complete governed executable Web verification of overlay applicability/render/update behavior and bind only when the governed Application runtime route becomes available; do not invent a route.; Target Foundation Stage/WP=N/A ΓÇö APPLICATION/WEB CROSS-WORKSTREAM CONTRACT; Review Trigger=governed Web verification; material Application overlay semantic change.`
